{# The layout every page of the shop extends, for the one thing they all need and none of them can state alone: dropping the wrapper an app's layout puts around a page's content, SiteBundle's ".container" and its 15px among them. Each template then states the page measure on what is its own, and only on that - a composed page's blocks carry the ".section-wrap" they already read, and a second one around them would apply its gutter twice, which is the very shape SiteBundle's pages/page.html.twig has. Nothing here names SiteBundle: this bundle requires c975l/core-bundle and not c975l/site-bundle, so the block name comes from UiBundle. The app's own file first, as SiteBundle's page does, so a site adding blocks around its layout has them apply to the shop's pages too; UiBundle's layout is the fallback for an app that has not run the scaffold #}
{% extends ['layout.html.twig', '@c975LUi/layout.html.twig'] %}

{# A catalog being set up is kept out of search engines for as long as it is: the banner warns the visitor, not the crawler, which would file an empty or unfinished shop and show it as such until its next visit. Set after the page's own "robots", which this overrides, and dropped the moment the switch is turned off #}
{% if config('shop-test-mode') %}
    {% set robots = 'noindex, follow' %}
{% endif %}

{# "parent()" is deliberately not called: it would render the wrapper of whichever layout sits between this one and UiBundle's, which is the very wrapper this block exists to drop #}
{% block container %}
    {% block content %}{% endblock %}
{% endblock %}
